            <h2> Explore Popular Places to Visit in <span>Islamabad</span></h2>
            <p>
                From natural wonders to historical icons, Islamabad is packed with stunning locations that showcase the city’s unique beauty and calm atmosphere. Islamabad is not just the political heart of Pakistan — it's also one of the most scenic, peaceful, and visitor-friendly cities in South Asia. Whether you're planning a relaxing holiday, a family getaway, or a business trip with some leisure on the side, this city has something for everyone. From lush green hills and historic landmarks to bustling markets and modern entertainment, Islamabad offers a perfect blend of nature, culture, and fun. At Mount Feast Hotels, we bring you closer to the best tourist attractions in Islamabad and guide you through the most popular activities for a memorable stay.
            </p>
            <div class="title-border">
                <div class="title-border-inner"></div>
                <div class="title-border-inner"></div>
                <div class="title-border-inner"></div>
                <div class="title-border-inner"></div>
                <div class="title-border-inner"></div>
                <div class="title-border-inner"></div>
                <div class="title-border-inner"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="slick row wow fadeInUp delay-04s"
             data-slick='{"slidesToShow": 3, "responsive":[{"breakpoint": 1024,"settings":{"slidesToShow": 2}}, {"breakpoint": 768,"settings":{"slidesToShow": 1}}]}'>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/Places & Activites/1.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">Faisal Mosque</a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            The Faisal Mosque is not only the largest mosque in Pakistan but also a globally
                            recognized architectural marvel. Designed in a unique, modern tent-like shape,
                            it stands at the foothills of the majestic Margalla Hills. Its vast courtyard,
                            elegant white marble structure, and tranquil ambiance make it a spiritual and
                            visual experience. The mosque accommodates over 100,000 worshippers and remains
                            one of the most photographed landmarks in Islamabad, drawing tourists, pilgrims,
                            and architecture enthusiasts from all over the world.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/Places & Activites/2.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">Daman-e-Koh</a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            A panoramic viewpoint located halfway up the Margalla Hills, Daman-e-Koh
                            offers awe-inspiring vistas of the city below. The area features landscaped
                            terraces, walking paths, and observation decks that make it a favorite for
                            families, couples, and nature enthusiasts. On a clear day, you can spot key
                            city landmarks, and during sunset, the whole skyline glows with a magical hue.
                            The route to Daman-e-Koh is lined with wildlife, and the location often serves
                            as the starting point for scenic treks.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/Places & Activites/3.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">Pakistan Monument</a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            Situated on the western Shakarparian Hills, the Pakistan Monument is a symbol of national
                            unity. Its petal-shaped structure, representing the four provinces and three territories
                            of Pakistan, makes it one of the most meaningful monuments in the country. The site also
                            includes the Pakistan Monument Museum, showcasing the rich history and sacrifices of the
                            nation’s founders. At night, the monument is beautifully lit, offering a peaceful and
                            patriotic atmosphere ideal for evening strolls and photos.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/Places & Activites/4.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">Lok Virsa Museum</a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            This cultural treasure trove is dedicated to preserving Pakistan’s rich and diverse heritage.
                            Lok Virsa Museum features stunning exhibits of traditional textiles, musical instruments, handicrafts,
                            pottery, and folk art from all regions of Pakistan. Live performances, workshops, and seasonal festivals
                            make it a vibrant cultural hub. The museum provides an engaging learning experience for all ages and is
                            one of the best ways to understand the heart and soul of Pakistani traditions.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/Places & Activites/5.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">Rawal Lake</a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            Tucked between the city and the Margalla Hills, Rawal Lake offers a natural
                            sanctuary perfect for relaxing getaways. The lake is a hub for recreational
                            activities including boating, jet-skiing, fishing, and lakeside dining. Families
                            can enjoy a peaceful picnic while kids play in the nearby Lake View Park. Birdwatchers
                            and photographers also flock to the lake to capture stunning views
                            of migratory birds, especially during golden hour and sunset.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/Places & Activites/6.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">Saidpur Village</a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            Blending history with hospitality, Saidpur Village is a restored Mughal-era hamlet nestled at the base
                            of the Margalla Hills. It features cobblestone paths, historic Hindu temples, a Gurdwara, and charming
                            cafés that serve traditional and continental food. The village is known for its art galleries, craft shops, and serene atmosphere, offering a unique fusion of heritage
                            and modern culture. It’s a great spot for a relaxing evening or a cultural photo walk.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/Places & Activites/7.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">Shakarparian Park</a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            Located at a strategic elevation between the twin cities, Shakarparian Park is a scenic and peaceful retreat filled with shady trees, flowerbeds, and historic significance. The park is known for hosting the Pakistan Monument and provides open green spaces ideal for picnics and family outings. It also offers walking trails and viewpoints with spectacular vistas of Islamabad and Rawalpindi. Several national events and cultural festivals are celebrated here, adding to its popularity.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/popular-places/centarus.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">
                                Centaurus Mall
                            </a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            As Islamabad's premier shopping and lifestyle destination, Centaurus Mall brings
                            luxury and convenience under one roof. Spread across multiple levels, the mall
                            features high-end brands, a massive food court, a multiplex cinema, indoor
                            amusement options for kids, and much more. Whether you're in the mood for a
                            shopping spree, a delicious meal, or just looking to spend time indoors, Centaurus
                            provides a complete entertainment package.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/Places & Activites/7.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">
                                Margalla Hills National Park
                            </a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            A nature lover’s dream, Margalla Hills National Park spans over 17,000 hectares 
                            and is part of the Himalayan foothills. It offers over six hiking trails with
                            varying difficulty levels, panoramic viewpoints, waterfalls, and diverse flora 
                            and fauna. From leopards and wild boars to exotic birds, the park is a haven 
                            for wildlife enthusiasts and adventure seekers alike. It also plays host to 
                            eco-tourism efforts, bird watching events, and conservation education programs.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/Places & Activites/8.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">
                                Dino Valley Islamabad
                            </a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            One of Islamabad’s newest and most popular family attractions, Dino Valley is a thrilling
                            dinosaur-themed amusement park located near the foothills of the Margalla range. The park 
                            features life-sized dinosaur models that move and roar, interactive educational experiences,
                            kids' play zones, and family-friendly dining options. It’s an ideal day-out destination for children
                            and parents alike and offers a blend of fun, learning, and natural beauty.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="item">
                <div class="popular-places-box-2">
                    <img src="../Content/Assets/img/Places & Activites/9.png"
                         alt="photo"
                         class="img-fluid w-100" />
                    <div class="ling-section">
                        <h3>
                            <a href="#">
                                Fatima Jinnah Park (F-9 Park)
                            </a>
                        </h3>
                        <p class="member-socials">
                            Spanning over 750 acres, Fatima Jinnah Park is one of the largest public parks
                            in Asia. It features vast green lawns, jogging tracks, fountains, walking paths, 
                            and recreational areas. The park is a fitness hub and picnic favorite among
                            locals, offering peace and open space in the heart of the city. Weekend bazaars
                            and open-air festivals are also hosted here.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="listings_no">Top Tourist Attraction</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
